---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base
  title="Stories from the Gorge"
  description="Stories behind photographs made by Ryan D. Lewis in Kentucky’s Red River Gorge and Clifty Wilderness."
>
  <div class="page prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Stories</p>
    <h1>Stories from the Gorge</h1>
    <p class="lede">The photographs on Red River Gorge Hiker come from particular days—weather changing, difficult winter travel, unexpected light, and long hours exploring the landscape.</p>

    <section>
      <h2>A rainbow after the storm</h2>
      <p>A hard summer rain cleared above Eagle’s Point Buttress and revealed a double rainbow across the Gorge while Ryan was preparing for a Sheltowee Trace thru-hike.</p>
      <a href={`${base}photographs/double-rainbow-at-eagles-point-buttress/`}>Read the full story</a>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Winter at Red-byrd Arch</h2>
      <p>Snow, ice, and freezing conditions changed the familiar sandstone shelter into a severe winter scene dominated by a large ice formation.</p>
      <a href={`${base}photographs/winter-at-red-byrd-arch/`}>Read the full story</a>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Discovering Splatter Falls</h2>
      <p>While exploring remote cliff-line drainages, Ryan found a four-drop cascade, measured and documented it, and named it Splatter Falls for the way the water bursts outward between its middle drops.</p>
      <a href={`${base}photographs/splatter-falls/`}>Read the full story</a>
    </section>

    <div class="notice">
      Detailed off-trail route information and sensitive coordinates are not published simply because a photograph was made there.
    </div>

    <p><a class="button" href={`${base}collection/`}>View all six photographs</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
